<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Torontál County</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Torontál County was a county of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a> in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banat">Banat</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisza">Tisza</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mures-river">Maros</a>, with its seat at Nagybecskerek, now Zrenjanin in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>. Re-established in 1779 when the civil Banat was returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, it had a mixed population of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, Germans, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanians">Romanians</a> and Hungarians. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> it was divided between the Kingdom of the Serbs, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> and Hungary, which kept a small part.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/torontal-county.jpg" alt="Torontál County" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hogweard · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Toront%C3%A1l_v%C3%A1rmegye_Magyarorsz%C3%A1gon.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
